<br/>
<br/>Many of the armor penetration items like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50633/sindragosas-cruel-claw">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterhorn_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Cruel Claw</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a> are technically best in slot for Assassination rogues but have very close alternatives. Because Assassination rogues deal a lot of magical damage that is not boosted by armor penetration the stat is slightly less valuable than it is for other classes. While it may be very difficult to get the full best in slot items, it should be very easy to get the very close second best options that other players don't want.<br/>
<br/>A change with Phase 4 is that your critical strike chance will start getting high enough that you'll need to check if you are going over the critical strike chance cap. This was only rarely an issue in Phase 2 or Phase 3 gear levels. The section on critical strike rating in the Stat Priority guide can tell you all about that, found here: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/combat-rogue-dps-stat-priority-and-attributes-wrath-of-the-lich-king-classic-16038">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Combat Rogue DPS Stat Priority and Attributes - Wrath of the Lich King Classic</span></a>. If you find yourself over your critical strike chance cap, swapping out attack power or haste gems for more hit rating gems is usually a good solution.<br/>
<br/>Almost all of the yellow gem slots are filled with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40159/stark-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stark Ametrine</span></a> this phase instead of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40157/pristine-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pristine Ametrine</span></a> like they were last phase. This is a extremely minor improvement in performance. Personally I suggest continuing to gem the Pristine Ametrines while gearing up so you are less likely to run into critical strike cap issues as you swap and upgrade armor pieces.<br/>
<br/>Many mail users, plate users, and strength classes have agility and leather items as their best in slot pieces this phase. It is often the case that these classes have mail, plate, or strength item alternatives in those slots that are not technically best in slot for them but are pretty close in performance. When figuring out loot distribution in your guild, you should consider what other options each player has especially for a hotly contested item where it is unlikely everyone who wants it will be able to get it.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Assassination Rogue DPS Phase 4</h3>You should absolutely prioritize getting four pieces of your tier set first with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a>. You'll need the 251 ilvl versions to upgrade into the 264, and you'll need the 264 ilvl version to upgrade into the best in slot 277 version. After that, none of the remaining items are BIS so you can prioritize different things based on what your own weakest gear slots are. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50474/shrapnel-star">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_throwingknife_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shrapnel Star</span></a> is pretty good, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50972/shadow-seekers-tunic">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_22.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadow Seeker's Tunic</span></a> can be a nice stand-in piece until you acquire <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50656/ikfiruss-sack-of-wonder">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_22.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ikfirus's Sack of Wonder</span></a>.<br/>
