<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="wrist">Wrist for Assassination Rogue DPS Phase 4</h3>While armor penetration is not a preferred stat for Assassination rogues, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50670/toskks-maximized-wristguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Toskk's Maximized Wristguards</span></a> simply has much more stats than any other option, making it the best bracer for Assassination rogues. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51820/vambraces-of-the-frost-wyrm-queen">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vambraces of the Frost Wyrm Queen</span></a> are a very close second option which I'd suggest trying to get as a back-up, since many classes want the Toskk's item.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Bracer Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57683/fur-lining-attack-power">
