<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="feet">Feet for Assassination Rogue DPS Phase 4</h3>The best <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50607/frostbitten-fur-boots">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frostbitten Fur Boots</span></a> and second best <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51856/taldarams-soft-slippers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Taldaram's Soft Slippers</span></a> boots are very similar in the stats they offer. The Frostbitten Fur Boots simply offer more stats than the slippers, putting them a fair bit ahead. If the rest of your gear allows you to equip <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49895/footpads-of-impending-death">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Footpads of Impending Death</span></a> without going over expertise cap, it can be a very good option but normally the expertise from chest and legs will prevent that from being true.<br/>
